By analysis, Zhongwen Li drew the following conclusions: When calculating Au & Ag recovery, people shall select appropriate calculation method only after accurately analyzing its own characteristics of the enterprise and looking into the scope of application of each calculation method. Generally speaking, equilibrium method was suitable for those enterprises with stable production, no big variations in beginning balance & ending balance, and small purchase/sales of semi-finished product and intermediate product. Otherwise continued multiplication method should be adopted. Only by selecting appropriate calculation method satisfying characteristics of the enterprise, calculation results can accurately reflect actual level of the recovery of the enterprise. 

###### **Conclusion** 

**(1)** Au & Ag losses in copper smelting process are completely in the form of mechanical entrainment. It is critical to increase Au & Ag recovery by decreasing mechanical entrainment. And it is helpful for increasing Au & Ag recovery by giving sufficient setting time for slag, selecting appropriate slag chemistry, increasing superheat temperature of slag, and increasing difference between specific gravity of matte and specific gravity of slag; 

(2) In the course of copper concentrate smelting and slag cleaning, Au & Ag recovery is proportional to the direct recovery of copper. Therefore, the efficient way for increasing Au & Ag recovery is always to decrease dust rate. Moreover, the influence of dust rate on Au & Ag recovery shall be considered when we compare advantages and disadvantages among different copper smelting technologies; 

(3) When Cu in copper matte is above 10%, Au and Ag can be absorbed completely. Blister copper is the best collecting agent for Au. But by using collecting agent, enrichment effect of Ag is nothing like enrichment effect of Au; 

